@database "research"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: research.guide 1.0 (30.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Research"
@{h1}Research

A web research agent. You ask a question; it searches, opens the pages
that matter, reads them, checks the surprising claims against a second
source and answers with the URLs it actually read. A question with
independent parts -- three libraries to compare, four claims to check -- it
splits over up to four sub-researchers that work in parallel.

The plugin is configuration only: two agents, their prompt and one skill.
It has no tools of its own; it uses the shared search and reading tools
(Tavily when a key is set, DuckDuckGo without one, the web scraper).

@{code}
For users
  @{"  Asking it  " link use}
  @{"  How it researches  " link method}
  @{"  Wide questions  " link wide}

For agents and developers
  @{"  Calling it from another agent  " link tool}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node use "Asking it"
@{h1}Asking it

In the web UI, pick @{b}research_agent@{ub} as the agent of a chat (see
@{" Choosing an agent " link scarabhive/agents}). From the command line:

@{code sh}
agent-cli chat --agent research_agent
agent-cli run --agent research_agent "What is the default texture filter in Godot 4?"
@{body}

A good question says what would count as an answer and whether the date
matters: "the current stable version of X and its release date" works
better than "X version".

@{h2}What you get back

@{bullet}The answer first, in plain sentences, in the language you asked in
-- whatever language the sources were in.
@{bullet}Then @{tt}Sources:@{utt}, one line per source: the URL and what it
supports. Only pages it opened; it is told never to construct or remember
a URL.
@{bullet}Numbers, versions and dates as the source has them, with a note
when a source is old or two sources disagree.
@{bullet}When it found nothing usable, it says so and what it tried.

@{h2}When it asks you

The agent may ask one question back (the @{" ask_user " link ask_user/main}
tool) when your question can be read in ways that lead to different
answers. Sub-researchers never ask; they answer the agent that started
them.

@{h2}Limits

@{table}
Limit | research_agent | sub-researcher
Steps per run | 40 | 25
Sub-researchers at a time | 4 per session | none
Wait for sub-researchers | 900 s | --
@{body}

A step is one LLM call with the tool calls it asks for. Forty covers a few
searches, three or four pages, one long page read in pieces and a
cross-check.
@endnode

@node method "How it researches"
@{h1}How it researches

The method is the @{tt}web-research@{utt} skill, which is part of the
agent's prompt on every run. In short:

@{bullet}@{b}Know the question.@{ub} What fact, from what kind of source, as
of when. A question that is really several is taken one part at a time.
@{bullet}@{b}Search two or three ways.@{ub} Rephrased with the field's own
vocabulary, with @{tt}site:@{utt} when it is clear who owns the fact, with the
year or version when recency matters.
@{bullet}@{b}Rank the sources.@{ub} The owner of the fact (official docs,
specification, repository, vendor page) first, then references that cite
it, then named experts, then blogs and forums -- those only to find a
stronger source. Two to four pages, not ten.
@{bullet}@{b}Read, do not skim.@{ub} A search snippet is a lead, not
evidence. Long pages are read in windows (@{tt}offset@{utt}) instead of
guessed from the first screen.
@{bullet}@{b}Cross-check@{ub} whatever decides the answer or surprised it.
Disagreement between strong sources is reported as such, with both URLs.
@{bullet}@{b}Stop@{ub} when the question is answered or the next search would
only repeat what it has.

@{h2}With or without a Tavily key

@{table}
 | search | read a page | read several at once
key set | tavily_search_web_search | web_scraper_page | tavily_search_extract
no key | duckduckgo_search_web_search | web_scraper_page | one page at a time
@{body}

Nothing in the prompt switches this: without @{tt}TAVILY_API_KEY@{utt} the
Tavily server offers no tools, so the agent only ever sees tools that work.
DuckDuckGo needs no account and returns titles and snippets only, so the
scraper does the reading.

@{h2}Blocked pages and files

A challenge page, a 403, 429 or 503 comes back from the scraper as an
error; the agent looks for the same content elsewhere instead of retrying.
A login or cookie wall comes back as the wall's own text. PDFs and other
files are not read as pages: @{tt}web_scraper_download@{utt} saves them into
@{tt}data/workspace@{utt} (see @{" Downloading a file " link web_scraper/download}).
The agent has no tool to read that file afterwards; other agents working
in the workspace can.
@endnode

@node wide "Wide questions"
@{h1}Wide questions

For a question with independent parts that each need their own searching
-- a comparison of several products, several claims to verify, several
ecosystems to survey -- the agent starts one @{b}research_worker@{ub} per
part without waiting, then waits for all of them once and merges their
answers and sources into its own. One fact or one page it researches
itself; branching costs a full prompt per branch.

@{h2}The worker

@{tt}research_worker@{utt} is the research agent minus three things:
@{bullet}no sub-agent manager, so a branch cannot branch again -- wherever
the research agent itself runs, from the UI or as another agent's
sub-agent;
@{bullet}no @{tt}ask_user@{utt}: its questions are the coordinator's to ask;
@{bullet}25 steps instead of 40, no Markdown formatting of its answer and
no list of running sub-agents.

It shares the prompt file; the section about branching is left out of its
prompt, so it is never told to use a tool it does not have.

@{h2}Limits

The manager (@{tt}research_sam@{utt}) may start only
@{tt}research_worker@{utt}, and at most 4 of them in a session that are not
archived (@{tt}max_sub_agents_per_type@{utt}; the session limit of 8 is never
reached with one type). A fifth archives the oldest to make room
(@{tt}auto_archive_on_limit@{utt}). A wait gives up after 900 seconds
(@{tt}default_wait_timeout@{utt}).

The agent sees a short list of its sub-researchers (the manager's
@{tt}inject_sub_agent_context@{utt} hook, at most 4 shown, archived ones left
out), appended as a turn at the end of the context whenever the list has
changed, so it waits for them instead of starting a second copy. See @{" Sub-agents and the SAM " link scarabhive/subagents}.
@endnode

@node tool "Calling it from another agent"
@{h1}Calling it from another agent

The agent is visible both in the UI and as a tool (@{tt}visibility:
both@{utt}). Another agent reaches it in one of two ways.

@{h2}As a tool

Put @{tt}"+research_agent/*"@{utt} into the caller's
@{tt}agent_config.tools.allowed@{utt}. The caller then has:

@{table}
Tool | What it does
research_agent_execute_task | runs the research agent on one task and returns its answer
research_agent_list_available_tools | lists the tools the research agent has (names and descriptions)
@{body}

Parameters of @{tt}research_agent_execute_task@{utt}:

@{table}
Name | Meaning
task | required; the question and what would count as an answer
llm_profile | optional; one of the agent's two routes, @{tt}or-deepseek-flash@{utt} or @{tt}deepseek-chat@{utt}
use_advanced_model | has no effect: the agent has no advanced profile
@{body}

@{h2}As a sub-agent

Add @{tt}research_agent@{utt} to the @{tt}allowed_agents@{utt} of the caller's
sub-agent manager and allow that manager's tools. The shared
@{tt}sub_agent_manager@{utt} in @{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt} already lists
it. A sub-agent keeps its history and can be continued with a follow-up
question. It can still branch into its own workers from there.

@{code}
sub_agent_manager_manage_sub_agent(operation="create", agent_type="research_agent",
    task="Which HTTP/2 features does aiohttp 3.x support? Official docs or source.")
@{body}
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}The prompt

@{tt}agents/prompts/research_agent.md@{utt}, read from disk on every run, so
an edit takes effect at once. It has four parts: the role and the list of
tools the agent has, which tool to search and read with, the method in five
steps, and how to write the answer. For @{tt}research_agent@{utt} it adds the
section on branching with the exact call:

@{code}
research_sam_manage_sub_agent(operation="create", agent_type="research_worker",
    task="<the sub-question>", blocking=false)
@{body}

followed by one @{tt}wait_all@{utt} with the @{tt}instance_ids@{utt} the creates
returned. The prompt ends with the date (day only). After it comes the full
@{tt}web-research@{utt} skill (@{tt}skills/web-research/SKILL.md@{utt}),
about 7,400 characters together; the worker's prompt, without the
branching section, about 6,800.

@{h2}Its tools

@{table}
Tool | From | Worker
tavily_search_web_search, tavily_search_extract | @{" tavily_search " link tavily_search/main}, only with a key | yes
duckduckgo_search_web_search | @{" duckduckgo_search " link duckduckgo_search/main} | yes
web_scraper_page, web_scraper_download | @{" web_scraper " link web_scraper/main} | yes
datetime_operations | datetime | yes
context_engineer_list, _read, _store_fact, _compact | @{" context_engineer " link context_engineer/main} | yes
research_sam_manage_sub_agent | this plugin's manager | no
ask_user | @{" ask_user " link ask_user/main} | no
@{body}

The descriptions are the tools' own. The agent's own tool, as another agent
sees it, carries the description from @{tt}self_tool_descriptions@{utt} in
@{tt}agents/research_agent.yaml@{utt}.

@{h2}Hooks that run for it

@{bullet}@{tt}context_engineer.engineer_context@{utt} -- trims old tool results
when the context grows (the 200,000-token window is set for all models).
See @{" The compaction hook " link context_engineer/hook}.
@{bullet}@{tt}research_sam.inject_sub_agent_context@{utt} -- the list of running
sub-researchers; off for the worker.

@{h2}Prompt cache

The system prompt is fixed for a run -- the date changes once a day, the
step counter is not in it -- and the agent runs with
@{tt}prompt_cache_mode: multi_turn@{utt}. The sub-researcher list is appended
at the end and rewrites nothing before it. What breaks the cached prefix is
the context engineer's compaction, which it does seldom and deep on
purpose.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

Nothing to enable: the files are found by convention.

@{table}
File | Picked up by
agents/research_agent.yaml | @{tt}config/config.yaml@{utt} includes @{tt}../src/plugins*/*/agents/*.yaml@{utt}
agents/research_worker.yaml | the same include
agents/tools.yaml | the same include; defines @{tt}research_sam@{utt}
agents/prompts/research_agent.md | @{tt}system_template@{utt}, relative to the YAML
skills/web-research/SKILL.md | @{tt}skills.skill_dirs@{utt} lists @{tt}src/plugins*/*/skills@{utt}
@{body}

@{h2}What it needs

The shared instances in @{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}, all enabled:
@{tt}duckduckgo_search@{utt}, @{tt}web_scraper@{utt} (with
@{tt}allowed_directories@{utt} for downloads), @{tt}datetime@{utt},
@{tt}ask_user@{utt}, @{tt}context_engineer@{utt};
and @{tt}tavily_search@{utt}, which offers tools only with a key:

@{code yaml}
tavily_search:
  type: tavily_search
  enabled: true
  api_key: "${TAVILY_API_KEY}"
@{body}

@{h2}The agent

@{table}
Key | Value | Meaning
type | multi_turn_agent | a basic agent with the context engineer, a 200k window and multi-turn caching
llm_profile | [or-deepseek-flash, deepseek-chat] | the chain; the second route takes over when the first fails
max_steps | 40 (worker 25) | step budget per run
skills.always | [web-research] | the method, in the prompt on every run
template_vars.can_fork | true (worker false) | renders the branching section of the prompt
visibility | both (worker tool) | UI and tool; the worker is not in the UI
@{body}

@{h2}The sub-agent manager (agents/tools.yaml)

@{table}
Key | Value | Default in code
allowed_agents | [research_worker] | --
max_sub_agents_per_type | 4 | 3
max_sub_agents_per_session | 8 | 10
max_nesting_depth | 5 | 5
max_message_history | 50 | 100
default_wait_timeout | 900 | 3600
auto_archive_on_limit | true | false
hook_config.inject_sub_agent_context | max_sub_agents_shown 4, show_completed false | 10, false
@{body}

@{h2}Tuning

@{table}
Want | Change
another model | @{tt}llm_profile@{utt} in @{tt}agents/research_agent.yaml@{utt}; keep two routes
deeper research | @{tt}max_steps@{utt}
another method | @{tt}skills/web-research/SKILL.md@{utt}
downloads elsewhere | @{tt}allowed_directories@{utt} of @{tt}web_scraper@{utt}
@{body}

The configuration is checked by @{tt}tests/test_research_config.py@{utt}:
the prompt as it renders, every tool it names, the skill's discovery, the
manager and the worker's missing manager.
@endnode
